# Data conversion between kilobyte and pebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kilobyte and pebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KB to 0.0000PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0000PiB; backward, converting 1PiB to 1125899906842.624KB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PiB yields 1688849860263.936KB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KB
print(forward_whole->to(PiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(forward_fractional->to(PiB))
backward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(backward_whole->to(KB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(backward_fractional->to(KB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PiB
0.0000PiB
1125899906842.624KB
1688849860263.936KB

<<< stderr
